    {
      "id": 7,
      "name": "R forecast subs[A,C]",
      "kind": "Aux",
      "equation": "((R Delayed subs[A]) * (1 + TREND(R Delayed subs[A], Fcst smoothing time subs[C], 0) * (Fcst horizon subs)))",
      "units": "widgets/Month",
      "comment": "The FORECAST function provides a very simple trend extrapolation forecast    of the future value of a variable based on its past behavior.  Like any    trend extrapolator it performs very badly at turnarounds. It is also    susceptible to noise amplification, though other extrapolators are more    robust to that issue.",
